<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Calculating Sine and Cosine Values Using a Calculator</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Use a calculator to compute the following sines and cosines. Give your answers correct to <strong>4 decimal places</strong>.</p>

<ol type="a">
  <li>
    <p>\(\sin({@a1@}^{\circ})=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>\(\sin({@a2@}^{\circ})=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>\(\cos({@a3@}^{\circ})=\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>\(\cos({@a4@}^{\circ})=\) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</p>
  </li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Worked Solution:</strong></p>

<p>Using a calculator, we evaluate the trigonometric functions and round each result to exactly 4 decimal places:</p>

<ol type="a">
  <li>
    <p>\(\sin({@a1@}^\circ) = {@disp_1@}\)</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>\(\sin({@a2@}^\circ) = {@disp_2@}\)</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>\(\cos({@a3@}^\circ) = {@disp_3@}\)</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <p>\(\cos({@a4@}^\circ) = {@disp_4@}\)</p>
  </li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
